According to http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asklepios and (to my own
memories of my early mythology-enthusiasm), Asklepios was not a god,
but a mortal who learned medicine from the gods; his success at
reviving the dead caused Zeus to kill him with a thunderbolt; after
which he was enshrined in the skies as the constellation Ophiuchus (the
serpent holder).



